ing  the search with help from other private  vessels in the area  it's not known why the boat capsized but  there were high winds in the area  when it went down people in the capital  of niger are mourning the deaths of 20  children after a devastating fire at an  elementary school  rows of burnt desks and chairs are all  that remain the flames broke out during  classes and authorities say  high winds fanned the flames spreading  them through the school  about 2 000 children attend classes  there investigators are working to  determine what caused the fire  it has highlighted the danger of  temporary classrooms  straw huts are often set up to make room  for students at overcrowded schools  [Music]  final countdown next canada's top  athletes prepare for tokyo's olympics  there's usually such a big buildup to  the summer olympics but this year things  are much  more muted the tokyo olympics already  postponed by year  start in just 100 days and for athletes  their families and for sports fans  this is going to be an olympics like no  other mike trolley  explains it's fair to say the road to  the tokyo olympics is lacking its usual  punch remember the torch run leading up  to vancouver  in japan a surge in kova 19 cases has  pushed runners  off public roads to make up for the lost  energy  they danced once the games begin there  will be some spectators in the stands  but they won't be allowed to cheer  kayaker maddie schmidt says  in a way they train for that during  olympic qualifications  we didn't have spectators there either  so we finished the race and it was like  a little golf clap  and it was so anticlimactic so if it's  if it's anything more than that i think  we're gonna be pretty used to it  what will be harder for athletes to  process is the isolation  as japan has said only members of team  canada can enter the country  family and friends have to stay at home  thank gosh  for you know live streaming and  face time and watch that video and zoom  like i fe